9. Overall System Operation
The system integrates power generation and storage, agricultural sensing, local control, irrigation, fire protection, and IoT communication.
• Power supply: The solar panel, battery, and power-regulation components supply electricity to the system.
• Data collection: Sensors measure soil and environmental conditions or detect fire-related signals.
• Processing: The ESP32 reads sensor inputs and executes the programmed control logic.
• Automatic action: The controller activates the appropriate irrigation or fire-response hardware when the programmed conditions are met.
• Communication: The configured software and IoT services transmit available data for remote monitoring.
• Offline response: Local fire-response logic can continue operating without the Internet, provided the controller, power supply, sensors, and response hardware remain functional.
